# linkedin-page-skills — optional configuration
#
# Nothing here is required. The bundle works with no configuration at all:
# approved drafts come back as paste blocks with the admin path.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT configurable here, on purpose:
#
#   LINKEDIN_PAGE_CUSTOM_POSTER
#
# This variable names a command that gets EXECUTED with an approved draft on
# stdin. It is read from the real shell environment only, and ignored when it
# appears in a .env file, because a file on disk choosing which executable runs
# is a code-execution hole dressed as configuration.
#
# To use it, export it in a trusted shell before starting the agent:
#   export LINKEDIN_PAGE_CUSTOM_POSTER='/path/to/your-poster'
#
# Only Page posts, document posts and comments can be published by any API.
# Articles, newsletters, polls, events and the static Page fields have no
# LinkedIn publishing API at all, so they are manual for everyone.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The Page's numeric id, if you want skills to stop asking for it.
# Find it in Page admin view, in the URL. A vanity slug is NOT this: lib
# refuses to convert one into an organization URN rather than guess, because a
# wrong id publishes somewhere nobody is watching.
# LINKEDIN_PAGE_ID=

# Nothing else. Analytics and keyword data come from connectors the session
# already has (Search Console, Ahrefs, Semrush), not from keys stored here.
